<p>The Trump administration has instructed US diplomats worldwide to press allied governments to designate Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps and Lebanon-based Hezbollah as terrorist organizations, according to an internal State Department cable dated March 16 and signed by Secretary of State Marco Rubio. The directive tells diplomats to raise the issue with foreign counterparts at the highest appropriate level by March 20, underscoring a coordinated push to rally partners behind Washington’s current military operation and broader pressure campaign. The cable says the request is driven by an elevated risk of attack, and the reports describe the effort as part of the administration’s wider push to line up support for its military operation and pressure campaign. Some allies have previously been reluctant to take that step.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/biMAfm6ATFMMKLjVzb-uNxt8CbimjPbnZlrIe3jZDvJHjiLvhbj8moTDByAxkPI51Kpf17jIfyQQVUwHaKlhOfoKY4eGtzg_BPGMbGumj8iqGPVEFcILM7zvAYBudj01_t_8-dGDZD_WkTda2hMopIvKdM5Am1cRbRbDYNlekNm18Jqy1_6XxYvlNg' alt='File image used with reporting on the US push to blacklist Iran’s Revolutionary Guards and Hezbollah' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Full overseas network: The directive went to US diplomatic and consular posts, not just embassies, showing that the department used its broader overseas footprint to carry the message.</li><li>Single regional file: By pairing the IRGC and Hezbollah in one request, Washington treated pressure on an Iranian state institution and a Lebanon-based armed group as part of the same regional campaign.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>State Department leadership: The internal cable frames the move around an elevated risk of attack, suggesting US officials see the designations as part of an immediate security response, not just a longer-term diplomatic goal. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/rubio-tells-us-diplomats-push-allies-blacklist-irans-revolutionary-guards-and'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>US allies: Reports that some partners have been reluctant suggest that domestic legal standards and regional diplomatic calculations could shape how far they are willing to mirror Washington’s designations. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/rubio-tells-us-diplomats-to-push-allies-to-blacklist-irans-revolutionary-guards-and-hezbollah'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-marco-rubio-urges-us-allies-to-blacklist-irans-military-hezbollah-11225379#publisher=newsstand'>US Urges Allies To Designate Iran&#x27;s Military, Hezbollah As Terrorist Groups</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/rubio-tells-us-diplomats-to-push-allies-to-blacklist-irans-revolutionary-guards-and-hezbollah'>Rubio tells US diplomats to push allies to blacklist Iran’s Revolutionary Guards and Hezbollah</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/rubio-tells-us-diplomats-push-allies-blacklist-irans-revolutionary-guards-and'>Rubio tells US diplomats to push allies to blacklist Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guards and Hezbollah</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/trump-administration-pushes-allies-to-blacklist-irgc-and-hezbollah-13990206.html'>Trump administration pushes allies to blacklist IRGC and Hezbollah</a> - firstpost.com</li></ul>